{
  "_about": {
    "name": "receipts-gt-10",
    "labelled_on": "2026-08-09",
    "source": "10 photographed Philippine retail/restaurant receipts (r1..r10)",
    "labeller": "Manual transcription from the source images, one pass per receipt, values read straight off the paper.",
    "policy": [
      "This is a TRANSCRIPTION ground truth, not an arithmetic one: the label is what is PRINTED, even where the receipt itself is wrong (see r4 vatable_sales).",
      "null means the field is not printed on that receipt at all. A null label is scored as a true negative when the model also returns null, and as a false positive when the model invents a value.",
      "`accept` lists alternative readings that are also defensible for a genuinely ambiguous or dual-labelled figure; any of them counts as correct.",
      "Money fields are compared to the cent. Text fields are compared after case/punctuation normalisation and count as correct if the label is contained in the answer or vice versa.",
      "Line items are matched greedily on amount first, then on description similarity."
    ]
  },

